From: arch-m4 project
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3-apple: release failed deferred-probe resources

The cable-triggered initial core probe runs after the Apple glue is bound.
Core errors unwind runtime PM and non-managed allocations, but their managed
MMIO reservation and PHY references otherwise survive until glue removal.
A following cable event then fails with EBUSY instead of retrying the core.

Scope core-probe devres in a group, releasing it on error and retaining its
resources on success. Reset only the embedded core structure so retry reacquires PHYs and does not
retain readiness flags or accumulate host-port counts. Preserve the persistent glue allocation, reset, Apple MMIO,
and role switch. This does not retry failed host initialization automatically.

Local candidate against Linux e9d2237cd064e6d086d938cd9c85e0c963cf7291 plus
Wallace force-host and arch-m4 cable-lifecycle patches.
Native USB enumeration remains unverified.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -172,6 +172,7 @@
 static int dwc3_apple_core_probe(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc)
 {
 	struct dwc3_probe_data probe_data = {};
+	void *probe_group;
 	int ret;
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&appledwc->lock);
@@ -184,10 +185,29 @@
 	probe_data.skip_core_init_mode = true;
 	probe_data.properties = DWC3_DEFAULT_PROPERTIES;
 
+	/*
+	 * The initial core probe runs after the glue driver has bound. A failed
+	 * cable-triggered probe must release its managed resources now rather
+	 * than retaining its MMIO reservation until the glue driver is removed.
+	 * Keep the glue allocation, reset and Apple register mapping outside
+	 * this group so another cable event can safely retry the initial probe.
+	 */
+	probe_group = devres_open_group(appledwc->dev, NULL, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!probe_group)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
 	ret = dwc3_core_probe(&probe_data);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		devres_release_group(appledwc->dev, probe_group);
+
+		/* Core probe already unwinds runtime PM and non-managed resources. */
+		memset(&appledwc->dwc, 0, sizeof(appledwc->dwc));
+		appledwc->dwc.dev = appledwc->dev;
 		return ret;
-
+	}
+
+	devres_close_group(appledwc->dev, probe_group);
+	devres_remove_group(appledwc->dev, probe_group);
 	appledwc->state = DWC3_APPLE_NO_CABLE;
 	return 0;
 }
